rk suit, white shirt, and blue tie while speaking at a podium.\n    *   Frame 27-30: A bald man is wearing a dark suit, white shirt, and red patterned tie.\n\n2.  **Multiple people in frame wearing suits:** While most frames focus on one person, Frame 17 shows the man in the suit addressing a group, and the context of the documentary (interviews, hearings, financial settings) implies suits are common attire for the subjects. The repeated appearance of different individuals in suits across multiple frames confirms this.\n\n3.  **Clear view of business attire:** The suits worn by the individuals in Frames 12-15, 17, 20, 21-26, and 27-30 are clearly visible and identifiable as standard business/professional attire (suit jackets, dress shirts, ties).\n\n4.  **Compare prevalence against other costume types:**\n    *   **Dresses:** Frame 16 shows a woman in a light blue turtleneck sweater. Frame 17 shows a woman in a white top (possibly a blouse or dress). These are not formal dresses.\n    *   **Sportswear/Swimwear:** There is no evidence of sportswear or swimwear in any of the 30 frames. The settings (government buildings, offices, stock exchange) and the professional context (interviews with economists, politicians, bankers) make such attire highly unlikely.\n    *   **Casual Wear:** Frame 11 shows a man in a dark collared shirt (not a suit). Frame 7 shows a person in a red top (blurry, but appears casual). Frame 8-10 show silhouettes or blurred figures, some possibly in dark coats, but not clearly identifiable as suits or casual wear. Frame 18-19 show a man in a light-colored jacket over a shirt, which could be considered business casual but not a full suit.\n\n**Conclusion:** Suits are the most common and clearly identifiable costume type among the key figures shown in these frames. The professional context of the documentary (finance, government, economics) strongly supports this, and the visual evidence across multiple frames confirms that suits are the dominant form of attire for the subjects being interviewed or shown in official capacities. Therefore, '1' (suit) is the correct answer.\n", "\n=== Batch 60-78 (18 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5345.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5346.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5347.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5348.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5349.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5350.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5351.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5352.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5353.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5354.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5355.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5356.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5357.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5358.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5359.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5360.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5361.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/EpMLAQbSYAw/frames/frame_5362.jpg\nVLM Response: **Answer: 1 (suit) is correct.**\n\n**Verification:**\n\n1.  **People wearing suits (jacket/trousers combination):** In every single frame (1-18), Jerome Powell is clearly visible wearing a dark suit jacket, a white dress shirt, and a tie. The person seated behind him (partially visible) is also wearing a dark suit jacket and a face mask, consistent with formal business attire.\n\n2.  **Multiple people in frame wearing suits:** While only two individuals are consistently visi