\u202f17); bearded man in blazer (frame\u202f20); **Jerome\u202fPowell** again (frames\u202f21‑26); bald man (frames\u202f27‑30) | All in dark suits, ties vary (blue, red, patterned) |\n| **5345‑5362** (Batch\u202f2) | **Jerome\u202fPowell** (continuous) plus a partially visible colleague behind him | Dark suits, both wearing ties; the colleague also has a face mask |\n\n**Character tracking**\n\n- **Jerome\u202fPowell** is the most persistent figure: first appears in frame\u202f11 (Batch\u202f0) and re‑appears in every subsequent batch (frames\u202f21‑26, 27‑30, and all 18 frames of Batch\u202f2). He is consistently dressed in a dark suit with a white shirt and a tie (blue, then red‑patterned).  \n- **Mohamed\u202fA.\u202fEl‑Erian** is seen only in frames\u202f9‑10 (Batch\u202f0) in a dark suit.  \n- Other men in suits appear briefly in the early trading‑floor shots (frames\u202f1‑5) and in the later interview segments (frames\u202f12‑15,\u202f17,\u202f20,\u202f27‑30).  \n- A few non‑suit outfits appear sparingly: a blue collared shirt (frames\u202f6‑8) and a dark casual shirt (frame\u202f11 of Batch\u202f1). These are isolated and never dominate the visual field.\n\n**Costume prevalence**\n\n- Suits are present in **≈\u202f20+ of the 78 frames**, often with multiple people wearing them simultaneously (e.g., frames\u202f1‑5,\u202f17).  \n- No dresses, sportswear, swimwear, or other costume categories appear at all.  \n- The occasional collared‑shirt shots are outliers and do not affect the overall distribution.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nThe visual evidence across the three batches makes it clear that the **dark business suit** is the dominant (and effectively sole) costume in this video segment. Consequently, answer **‘1\u202f–\u202fsuit’** is the correct classification.', 'failed_images': []}
